Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-10 (engine run A's design,
section 10), no third-party content but KiCad's Device:R as the unnumbered
fixture carries it: a two-layer board, 20 by 20 mm (an Edge.Cuts rectangle),
with R1 and R2 in 0603 and these findings on purpose:
- a clearance: the VCC track (net class Power, by the pattern VCC in the
  project file) runs 0.15 mm above R1 pad 1 (SIG), against the custom rule
  "Tight" of drc-small.kicad_dru (A.NetClass == 'Power', clearance at least
  0.25 mm; the track is the rule's A in KiCad's track test);
- a connection not made: R1 pad 1 and R2 pad 2 share SIG, unrouted;
- a footprint with no symbol: R2 is on the board, not on the schematic (the
  schematic holds R1 alone, between the global labels SIG and VCC);
- an excluded finding with its comment: the VCC stub below R2 pad 1 ends in
  nothing (track_dangling), excluded in the project file;
plus a board text, a copper area (no net, B.Cu, never filled in the file, so
a check that fills makes one undo step) and the project file's severities:
the two library-original checks and isolated copper turned off.
ids.json names the items' uuids for the tests. The KiCad files carry no
comment (their formats have none), so this file holds their license.
